(function(){window.PhysicaRankPyqNeet_botany_plantgrowthanddevelopment=[{id:"neet-2026r-q101",pn:101,y:"Re-NEET 2026 \xB7 21 Jun",tp:"Plant Growth and Development",st:"Arithmetic growth",q:"Length of the stem at time 0 is 20 cm. The arithmetic growth rate is 30 cm per day. What is the length of the stem at the end of the 7\u1D57\u02B0 day?",o:["170 cm","230 cm","460 cm","50 cm"],c:1,s:`Arithmetic growth: L\u209C = L\u2080 + rt.
Here L\u209C = length at time t, L\u2080 = length at time zero, r = growth rate.
L(7th day) = 20 + 30 \xD7 7
= 20 + 210
= 230 cm.
So the stem is 230 cm long at the end of the 7\u1D57\u02B0 day.`},{id:"neet-2026-q103",pn:103,y:"NEET 2026 \xB7 3 May",tp:"Plant Growth and Development",st:"Phases of growth",q:"Which one of the following is not a characteristic of plant cells in the phase of elongation?",o:["Increased vacuolation","Large conspicuous nuclei","Cell enlargement","New cell wall deposition"],c:1,s:`The phase of elongation shows new cell wall deposition, increased vacuolation and cell enlargement.
Large conspicuous nuclei are a feature of cells in the meristematic phase, so (2) is not a characteristic of elongation.`},{id:"neet-2026-q111",pn:111,y:"NEET 2026 \xB7 3 May",tp:"Plant Growth and Development",st:"Plasticity",q:"Heterophyllous development in response to environment is an example of which of the following phenomena?",o:["Dedifferentiation","Elasticity","Redifferentiation","Plasticity"],c:3,s:`Plants follow different pathways in response to environment or phases of life to form different kinds of structures.
This ability is called plasticity, for example heterophylly in cotton, coriander and larkspur.`},{id:"neet-2026r-q115",pn:115,y:"Re-NEET 2026 \xB7 21 Jun",tp:"Plant Growth and Development",st:"Gibberellin",q:"Which of the following plant growth regulators promotes internode elongation prior to flowering in cabbage?",o:["Gibberellin","Indole butyric acid","Ethephon","Abscisic acid"],c:0,s:"Gibberellin promotes internode elongation prior to flowering in cabbage."},{id:"neet-2026r-q125",pn:125,y:"Re-NEET 2026 \xB7 21 Jun",tp:"Plant Growth and Development",st:"Plant growth regulators",q:"Which of the following plant growth regulators is used as herbicide?",o:["Kinetin","Abscisic acid","Gibberellin","2, 4-D"],c:3,s:`2, 4-D is an artificial auxin.
It is widely used as a herbicide.`},{id:"neet-2026-q126",pn:126,y:"NEET 2026 \xB7 3 May",tp:"Plant Growth and Development",st:"Plant growth regulators",q:`Match List-I (Growth Regulator) with List-II (Function/Effect):
A. 2,4-D \u2014 I. Brewing industry
B. GA\u2083 \u2014 II. Stimulation of stomatal closure
C. Kinetin \u2014 III. Herbicide
D. ABA \u2014 IV. Nutrient mobilisation
Choose the correct answer from the options given below:`,o:["A-IV, B-III, C-II, D-I","A-I, B-II, C-IV, D-III","A-III, B-I, C-IV, D-II","A-I, B-IV, C-III, D-II"],c:2,s:`2,4-D (an auxin) is a herbicide, so A-III.
GA\u2083 (gibberellic acid) is used in the brewing industry, so B-I.
Kinetin (a cytokinin) helps nutrient mobilisation, so C-IV.
ABA (abscisic acid) stimulates stomatal closure, so D-II.`},{id:"neet-2025-q108",pn:108,y:"NEET 2025",tp:"Plant Growth and Development",st:"Cytokinins, delay of senescence",q:"Which one of the following phytohormones promotes nutrient mobilization which helps in the delay of leaf senescence in plants?",o:["Ethylene","Abscisic acid","Gibberellin","Cytokinin"],c:3,s:`Cytokinins help to overcome apical dominance.
They promote nutrient mobilisation, which helps in the delay of leaf senescence.`},{id:"neet-2025-q173",pn:173,y:"NEET 2025",tp:"Plant Growth and Development",st:"Plant growth regulators",q:`Read the following statements on plant growth and development.
(A) Parthenocarpy can be induced by auxins.
(B) Plant growth regulators can be involved in promotion as well as inhibition of growth.
(C) Dedifferentiation is a pre-requisite for re-differentiation.
(D) Abscisic acid is a plant growth promoter.
(E) Apical dominance promotes the growth of lateral buds.`,o:["A, B, C only","A, C, E only","A, D, E only","B, D, E only"],c:0,s:`ABA is a plant growth inhibitor and an inhibitor of plant metabolism.
Apical dominance promotes growth of the apical bud.
Statements A, B and C are correct.`},{id:"neet-2024-q107",pn:107,y:"NEET 2024 \xB7 5 May",tp:"Plant Growth and Development",st:"Dedifferentiation",q:"Formation of interfascicular cambium from fully developed parenchyma cells is an example for",o:["Dedifferentiation","Maturation","Differentiation","Redifferentiation"],c:0,s:`Fully differentiated parenchyma cells regain the ability to divide and form interfascicular cambium.
This process is called dedifferentiation.`},{id:"neet-2024-q113",pn:113,y:"NEET 2024 \xB7 5 May",tp:"Plant Growth and Development",st:"Totipotency",q:"The capacity to generate a whole plant from any cell of the plant is called :",o:["Differentiation","Somatic hybridization","Totipotency","Micropropagation"],c:2,s:"Totipotency is the capacity to generate a whole plant from any cell of the plant."},{id:"neet-2024-q127",pn:127,y:"NEET 2024 \xB7 5 May",tp:"Plant Growth and Development",st:"Auxin applications",q:"Auxin is used by gardeners to prepare weed free lawns. But no damage is caused to grass as auxin;",o:["does not affect mature monocotyledonous plants.","can help in cell division in grasses, to produce growth.","promotes apical dominance.","promotes abscission of mature leaves only."],c:0,s:`Auxin does not affect mature monocot plants.
In grasses (monocots) externally applied auxin is translocated only to a limited extent and is quickly broken down.
So the lawn grass is not damaged.`},{id:"neet-2024-q139",pn:139,y:"NEET 2024 \xB7 5 May",tp:"Plant Growth and Development",st:"Plant growth regulators",q:"Spraying sugarcane crop with which of the following plant growth regulators, increases the length of stem, thus, increasing the yield?",o:["Cytokinin","Abscisic acid","Auxin","Gibberellin"],c:3,s:`Sugarcane stores carbohydrate as sugar in its stem.
Spraying sugarcane with gibberellins increases stem length, so the yield rises.`},{id:"neet-2023-q108",pn:108,y:"NEET 2023 \xB7 7 May",tp:"Plant Growth and Development",st:"Gibberellins: physiological effects",q:"Spraying of which of the following phytohormone on juvenile conifers helps in hastening the maturity period, that leads to early seed production ?",o:["Abscisic acid","Indole-3-butyric acid","Gibberellic acid","Zeatin"],c:2,s:`Spraying gibberellins on young conifers shortens the time to maturity.
This leads to early seed production.`},{id:"neet-2023-q109",pn:109,y:"NEET 2023 \xB7 7 May",tp:"Plant Growth and Development",st:"Differentiation and dedifferentiation",q:"In tissue culture experiments, leaf mesophyll cells are 'put in a culture medium to form callus. This phenomenon may be called as :",o:["Senescence","Differentiation","Dedifferentiation","Development"],c:2,s:`Mesophyll cells forming callus in culture is called dedifferentiation.
In dedifferentiation, living differentiated cells that had lost the ability to divide regain it under certain conditions.`},{id:"neet-2023-q124",pn:124,y:"NEET 2023 \xB7 7 May",tp:"Plant Growth and Development",st:"Ethylene: physiological effects",q:"Which hormone promotes internode/petiole elongation in deep water rice?",o:["2, 4-D","GA3","Kinetin","Ethylene"],c:3,s:"Ethylene promotes fast internode and petiole elongation in deep water rice."},{id:"neet-2022-q108",pn:108,y:"NEET 2022 \xB7 17 Jul",tp:"Plant Growth and Development",st:"Ethylene",q:"The gaseous plant growth regulator is used in plants to :",o:["promote root growth and roothair formation to increase the absorption surface","help overcome apical dominance","kill dicotyledonous weeds in the fields","speed up the malting process"],c:0,s:`Ethylene is the gaseous hormone.
It promotes lateral roots, adventitious roots and root hair growth.
Cytokinin overcomes apical dominance, auxin kills dicot weeds, gibberellin speeds malting.`},{id:"neet-2022r-q111",pn:111,y:"Re-NEET 2022 \xB7 4 Sep",tp:"Plant Growth and Development",st:"Plasticity",q:"The ability of plants to follow different pathways in response to environment leading to formation of different kinds of structures is called :",o:["Differentiation","Redifferentiation","Development","Plasticity"],c:3,s:`Plasticity is the ability of plants to follow different developmental pathways in response to the environment.
This gives different kinds of structures.`},{id:"neet-2022-q112",pn:112,y:"NEET 2022 \xB7 17 Jul",tp:"Plant Growth and Development",st:"Plasticity",q:"Which one of the following plants does not show plasticity?",o:["Coriander","Buttercup","Maize","Cotton"],c:2,s:`Plasticity is the ability of plants to form different structures in response to environment or life phase.
Heterophylly in cotton, coriander and larkspur is an example.
Maize does not show it.`},{id:"neet-2022r-q114",pn:114,y:"Re-NEET 2022 \xB7 4 Sep",tp:"Plant Growth and Development",st:"Plant growth regulators",q:"Which of the following growth regulators is an adenine derivative ?",o:["Abscisic acid","Auxin","Cytokinin","Ethylene"],c:2,s:`Cytokinin is an adenine derivative.
Auxin comes from the amino acid tryptophan.
Abscisic acid comes from violaxanthin.
Ethylene is a gas made from methionine.`},{id:"neet-2022-q117",pn:117,y:"NEET 2022 \xB7 17 Jul",tp:"Plant Growth and Development",st:"Ethylene",q:"Production of Cucumber has increased manifold in recent years. Application of which of the following phytohormones has resulted in this increased yield as the hormone is known to produce female flowers in the plants :",o:["Gibberellin","Ethylene","Cytokinin","ABA"],c:1,s:`Ethylene increases female flowers and fruits in plants like cucumber.
Gibberellins increase fruit size in some plants.`},{id:"neet-2022r-q117",pn:117,y:"Re-NEET 2022 \xB7 4 Sep",tp:"Plant Growth and Development",st:"Dedifferentiation",q:"The phenomenon by which the undividing parenchyma cells start to divide mitotically during plant tissue culture is called as :",o:["Secondary growth","Differentiation","Dedifferentiation","Redifferentiation"],c:2,s:"Undividing cells that start dividing mitotically again show dedifferentiation."}]})();
